 Because `frai-core` is a regular ESM package, you can import only the modules you need and embed FRAI capabilities inside automation pipelines, CI jobs, or custom products.
 
+### Evaluation with Thresholds
+
+Gate evaluation metrics on minimum scores to fail CI when quality drops:
+
+```ts
+import { Eval } from 'frai-core';
+
+const evaluations = Eval.runEvaluations({
+  outputs: ['Hello World'],
+  references: ['hello world']
+});
+
+const report = Eval.generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  outputsPath: 'outputs.json',
+  referencesPath: 'refs.json',
+  thresholds: { exact_match: 0.9, toxicity: 0.95 }
+});
+
+if (!report.passed) {
+  console.error('Thresholds failed:', report.thresholds);
+  process.exit(1);
+}
+```
+
+Thresholds accept:
+- An object: `{ exact_match: 0.9 }` where values are 0-1.
+- A metric with no score fails its threshold (instead of crashing or passing).
+- `report.passed` is true only if all thresholds pass (or no thresholds set).
+- `report.thresholds` is an array of `{ metric, min, score, passed }` entries.
+
